{
 "_source": "Computed by Civitas with Cook's formula from open precinct returns: 2020, the Voting and Election Science Team's precinct results and shapefiles (Harvard Dataverse doi:10.7910/DVN/K7760H, CC BY 4.0); 2024, the MIT Election Data and Science Lab's precinct returns (github.com/MEDSL/2024-elections-official, CC0), with listed errors corrected from state and county certified canvasses; U.S. Census Bureau 2020 blocks and block equivalency files.",
 "_method": "lean = -100 * (0.25 * (D20/(D20+R20) - N20) + 0.75 * (D24/(D24+R24) - N24)), positive = R lean; N = the national two-party Democratic share (MEDSL state returns). 2020 precinct votes shared among the Census blocks inside each precinct by population; 2024 precincts counted in the House district each voted in (2024 was held on the 119th Congress's lines); the 120th lines in states that redrew by swing transfer within county x 119th-district cells.",
 "_sign": "positive = R lean, negative = D lean (matches district_pvi.json)",
 "_window": "2020+2024",
 "_as_of": "2026-10-15",
 "_regenerate": "backend/scripts/build_district_lean.py",
